A git diff whose first hunk ends in blank context lines right before the
next @@. git reads every line up to a header as part of the hunk before it,
so those blanks are not ambiguous and must come back counted in after the
counts are scrambled. See test/corpus.ts.

diff --git a/mod.py b/mod.py
index 9418415..b81cef5 100644
--- a/mod.py
+++ b/mod.py
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
 def first():
-    return 1
+    return 10
 
 
@@ -8,4 +8,4 @@ def second():
 
 def third():
-    return 3
+    return 30
 
